in{aligned}4x-2y & =6 \\\\ -2y & =-4x+6 \\\\ y & =2x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $2.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $2$ is $y=2x+6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ea92f20-abc3-55e6-9cb0-e212a4501b51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501577} {:answer/id #uuid "61fe2478-10d2-5bca-920d-9f0daaf0b6ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501649} {:answer/id #uuid "7f128d65-7d5f-525e-9edd-3162254412a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=22x-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501705} {:answer/id #uuid "ed89ed12-51bd-556e-b4ad-ed83525eab09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501943} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b5fe75-82cb-53ca-9624-82b3c3a6b868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61fe2478-10d2-5bca-920d-9f0daaf0b6ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501649} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2adee77-1817-5967-af7e-f4bab1e9df6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502052}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9815706a-98d4-5baf-aff8-15181269835f" :question/math-academy-id "q-44382" :question/problem "A line $l$ is parallel to $4x-y=22.$  A possible equation for $l$ is" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $4x-y=22,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-y & =22 \\\\ -y & =-4x+22 \\\\ y & =4x-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $4.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $4$ is $y=4x+8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502137 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63aec5ed-70dd-568a-b800-b96182667ad1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{12}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501651} {:answer/id #uuid "6b220cef-1e57-5c7c-b8c9-140cde054ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501665} {:answer/id #uuid "73ec87cf-5e2f-5cab-8bf8-4edb168c5394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501678} {:answer/id #uuid "7f25e14f-dfb9-523c-b53b-932d5481661c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-12x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501706} {:answer/id #uuid "c722783d-27d3-5cb8-8edc-899b5962a24e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{3}x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b220cef-1e57-5c7c-b8c9-140cde054ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501665} :answer-field/id #uuid "04d55a55-dcb2-5f1f-bb49-f359d2f4f066" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501977}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b444fd71-00fa-57c3-8df1-8666ae2725d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-44380" :question/problem "A line $l$ is parallel to $6x-2y=11.$ A possible equation for $l$ is" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $6x-2y=11,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-2y & =11 \\\\ \\frac{6}{2}x-\\frac{2}{2}y & =\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ 3x-y & =\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ -y & =-3x+\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ y & =3x-\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $3.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $3$ is $y=3x-8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fee57e6-07c5-5eeb-be77-4e84bfcde73f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{3}x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714023} {:answer/id #uuid "4936341d-e3f6-5b00-8f8c-875e6bd0825c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714028} {:answer/id #uuid "5d04c2eb-fcc9-5dd9-a3bb-18ee16a9df8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714031} {:answer/id #uuid "639555c7-a7d9-5e51-8387-670d3be908be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714032} {:answer/id #uuid "ae6e7269-c355-5af5-8c85-b798fe30e4ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "639555c7-a7d9-5e51-8387-670d3be908be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714032} :answer-field/id #uuid "5418db33-c311-5320-b796-6820dd758fab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714029}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57d2a029-b35e-5d38-9b2b-8dac94881bf9" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is parallel to $3x-y=4$?" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $3x-y=4$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x-y &=4 \\\\\n-y &=-3x+4 \\\\\ny &=3x-4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the slope is $3$.\n\nOnly $y=3x+2$ has slope $3$. The other choices have slopes $-3$, $\\frac{1}{3}$, $1$, and $4$. Its $y$-intercept is $2$, different from $-4$, so it is a distinct parallel line.\n\nTherefore, choose $y=3x+2$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a8ce17d-056c-5084-9b79-95a17e0a43c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-3y=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714024} {:answer/id #uuid "3f577094-e3f6-5ea1-bc6a-21f0b17f65f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2y=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714026} {:answer/id #uuid "87bd287b-c116-5789-8f7c-762c0b632eaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+6y=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714033} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac3f5a0-3022-53c6-adfd-aa4165585955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+6y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714034} {:answer/id #uuid "d7285937-7614-5a8b-8c39-e1eb2f60012d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+2y=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ac3f5a0-3022-53c6-adfd-aa4165585955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+6y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714034} :answer-field/id #uuid "07040ff6-14f5-511a-b087-98694663c953" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714022}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b5956a25-ae04-54e4-95df-23c07e5d2820" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is parallel to $2x+3y=6$?" :question/worked-solution "Parallel lines have the same slope. First convert the given line to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x+3y &=6 \\\\\n3y &=-2x+6 \\\\\ny &=-\\frac{2}{3}x+2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required slope is $-\\frac{2}{3}$. The choices are also in standard form, so isolate $y$ to compare their slopes:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x+2y=9 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{9}{2} \\\\\n4x+6y=-6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-1 \\\\\n2x-3y=6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{2}{3}x-2 \\\\\n2x+6y=6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{1}{3}x+1 \\\\\n3x-2y=9 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{9}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOnly $4x+6y=-6$ has slope $-\\frac{2}{3}$. Its $y$-intercept is $-1$, different from $2$, so it is a distinct parallel line.\n\nTherefore, choose $4x+6y=-6$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3007bd26-05f0-535b-8f2b-f5431a57f779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-4y=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714025} {:answer/id #uuid "46304219-5f0d-54c4-9bac-54ebd6d22e4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+2y=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714027} {:answer/id #uuid "ca341d1e-4914-5613-b815-ef5e3fb3938a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-3y=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714038} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b90b3d-6bed-5fe6-bae7-1332416a8784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-2y=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714039} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f49538-7409-5703-bfcc-2c53509ffcc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+4y=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8f49538-7409-5703-bfcc-2c53509ffcc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+4y=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714042} :answer-field/id #uuid "daf5d20e-3e55-57e1-a8fc-b85c3db24317" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714041}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c8e04bf5-c2ee-52c5-9037-dd7593cea6e9" :question/problem "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $3x-2y=6$?" :question/worked-solution "Parallel lines are distinct lines with the same slope. Convert the given line to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x-2y &=6 \\\\\n-2y &=-3x+6 \\\\\ny &=\\frac{3}{2}x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow rewrite each choice:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x-4y=12 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{2}x-3 \\\\\n-6x+4y=8 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{2}x+2 \\\\\n3x+2y=6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{2}x+3 \\\\\n2x-3y=6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{2}{3}x-2 \\\\\n6x-2y=6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=3x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equations $6x-4y=12$ and $-6x+4y=8$ both have slope $\\frac{3}{2}$. But $6x-4y=12$ is just twice the original equation: it describes the same line, with the same $y$-intercept of $-3$. It is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe equation $-6x+4y=8$ has slope $\\frac{3}{2}$ and $y$-intercept $2$. It describes a different line with the same slope. The other three choices have different slopes.\n\nTherefore, choose $-6x+4y=8$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fa71151-8c33-53e2-bd7d-e203356e663a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714392} {:answer/id #uuid "a45a0b91-95e9-55f0-8117-168110cadb2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714394} {:answer/id #uuid "b29859c4-e972-54b7-91d4-d91732416ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-6x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714396} {:answer/id #uuid "c0911aa7-ad6f-540e-988b-1a6b0b96eb6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714397} {:answer/id #uuid "e446ba6b-6f63-560f-b58a-7f66ea5f8f40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fa71151-8c33-53e2-bd7d-e203356e663a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714392} :answer-field/id #uuid "8395b6a5-f666-5527-be2a-d43769e300f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714386}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12210ca3-e2dd-55be-9d40-51562d14a610" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is parallel to $9x-3y=-15$?" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $9x-3y=-15$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9x-3y &= -15 \\\\\n-3y &= -9x-15 \\\\\ny &= 3x+5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $3$.\n\nOnly $y=3x-2$ has slope $3$.\n\nThe line $y=3x-2$ has slope $3$ and $y$-intercept $-2$, different from $5$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\ny=3x-2\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25479a9a-9fa2-5797-a8c1-98da21b9f360" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-6x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714374} {:answer/id #uuid "3ec2122d-c865-50d7-94af-ae7a33043148" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714378} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab3b5a0-f10c-58ad-9d4e-41e43773df19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714385} {:answer/id #uuid "910b94d9-96df-5b16-9644-04bc3c57f27a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714388} {:answer/id #uuid "981e096e-bb30-5fbf-aece-3dafb219bed1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "981e096e-bb30-5fbf-aece-3dafb219bed1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714391} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd2cc84-5c32-542f-9c43-336148b7da21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 175