 "Which of the following lines is parallel to $-12x-2y=-8$?" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $-12x-2y=-8$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x-2y &= -8 \\\\\n-2y &= 12x-8 \\\\\ny &= -6x+4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-6$.\n\nOnly $y=-6x-2$ has slope $-6$.\n\nThe line $y=-6x-2$ has slope $-6$ and $y$-intercept $-2$, different from $4$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\ny=-6x-2\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b1f1bbc-482a-55ae-a664-466a7b4139aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-6x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714375} {:answer/id #uuid "5d477b80-c7b4-59c0-810e-5b9d5c5d548f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714382} {:answer/id #uuid "97f8d261-7e8e-5098-ba13-01fdc7ecf59c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714390} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a3b943-60a5-5e6e-a69c-47b469565b5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714403} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f4a594-be7b-5dca-ae6e-f11ddba3136c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97f8d261-7e8e-5098-ba13-01fdc7ecf59c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714390} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3e96f02-c8ad-5ad9-9e92-33ebfd7009ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714393}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ccc2465d-f7a4-5b30-a005-df94483fcf75" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is parallel to $6x+3y=-6$?" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $6x+3y=-6$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x+3y &= -6 \\\\\n3y &= -6x-6 \\\\\ny &= -2x-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-2$.\n\nOnly $y=-2x+5$ has slope $-2$.\n\nThe line $y=-2x+5$ has slope $-2$ and $y$-intercept $5$, different from $-2$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\ny=-2x+5\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714460 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a7ccf74-0366-54b1-b8c9-5657f91ec687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12x-2y=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714447} {:answer/id #uuid "6d5c6e30-d17f-5f5e-8eea-56489f8d1ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+8y=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714453} {:answer/id #uuid "71abddd0-a8cc-5bf1-84d0-8be26937566b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+12y=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714455} {:answer/id #uuid "c64ba7d8-071f-58eb-b8c3-c9b23c291a00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+12y=-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714463} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c4c9d8-a14f-5e5d-b6db-773c5138d377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18x-3y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a7ccf74-0366-54b1-b8c9-5657f91ec687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12x-2y=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714447} :answer-field/id #uuid "77e1c8f2-dd7d-57cb-a9bc-8395d74bd976" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714456}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aefd6738-17b4-5ae3-9465-79de326525f7" :question/problem "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $-12x-2y=-4$?" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $-12x-2y=-4$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x-2y &= -4 \\\\\n-2y &= 12x-4 \\\\\ny &= -6x+2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-6$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x-2y=8 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-6x-4 \\\\\n9x+12y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{4}x-2 \\\\\n-18x-3y=-6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-6x+2 \\\\\n9x+12y=-36 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{4}x-3 \\\\\n-6x+8y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{4}x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $-18x-3y=-6$ has both the same slope $-6$ and the same $y$-intercept $2$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $-12x-2y=8$ has slope $-6$ and $y$-intercept $-4$, different from $2$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n-12x-2y=8\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d912272-ed04-5b5d-97a0-256c5129cf71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18x-3y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714448} {:answer/id #uuid "3b71a58d-00cc-59cf-8d02-aab0f64ba0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+12y=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714450} {:answer/id #uuid "70bc2537-709e-558f-8157-9dbf9abbc9fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+12y=-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714454} {:answer/id #uuid "a52f0fa5-3ef4-5a11-a809-f3a5eeb857a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12x-2y=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714458} {:answer/id #uuid "fb2f2944-ac76-52f5-afac-d34d92645d4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+8y=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b71a58d-00cc-59cf-8d02-aab0f64ba0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+12y=-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714450} :answer-field/id #uuid "622ce8f8-220f-5994-aff3-dd6128157202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714452}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b7b90b87-1386-550b-b6ee-d5c0054b9d88" :question/problem "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $3x+4y=-12$?" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $3x+4y=-12$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x+4y &= -12 \\\\\n4y &= -3x-12 \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{3}{4}x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-\\frac{3}{4}$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x-2y=8 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-6x-4 \\\\\n9x+12y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{4}x-2 \\\\\n-18x-3y=-6 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-6x+2 \\\\\n9x+12y=-36 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{3}{4}x-3 \\\\\n-6x+8y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{4}x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $9x+12y=-36$ has both the same slope $-\\frac{3}{4}$ and the same $y$-intercept $-3$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $9x+12y=-24$ has slope $-\\frac{3}{4}$ and $y$-intercept $-2$, different from $-3$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n9x+12y=-24\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186714466 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf789df-bdf1-52e2-88ac-ddacc9cdbe14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12x-2y=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714445} {:answer/id #uuid "2e182e50-917d-50a6-8087-f99144feee97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+12y=-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186714449} {:answer/id #uuid "44a46405-8fa2-56be-bc48-aa0a2701