} :answer/value "-x+2y=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718303} {:answer/id #uuid "1047c200-142c-548b-a6e6-a282f50841d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x-9y=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718304} {:answer/id #uuid "28050f9d-3b2e-51d0-8263-2bd30107e170" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+2y=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718306} {:answer/id #uuid "7cdacb6c-45cc-59cc-aae4-1c5d7efe572e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x-6y=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718308} {:answer/id #uuid "86a15af6-11c2-51d1-a5e8-5e26b9737101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+2y=-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cdacb6c-45cc-59cc-aae4-1c5d7efe572e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x-6y=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718308} :answer-field/id #uuid "13de8c06-ac20-53f6-ad85-9c8c5fcb1d1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718305}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3b78d449-92e4-5521-a888-ec321cc21566" :question/problem "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $2x+3y=-3$?" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $2x+3y=-3$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x+3y &= -3 \\\\\n3y &= -2x-3 \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{2}{3}x-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-\\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x+2y=2 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{1}{2}x+1 \\\\\n-4x-6y=24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-4 \\\\\n-6x-9y=9 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-1 \\\\\n-3x+2y=-10 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{3}{2}x-5 \\\\\n-x+2y=-2 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{1}{2}x-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $-6x-9y=9$ has both the same slope $-\\frac{2}{3}$ and the same $y$-intercept $-1$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $-4x-6y=24$ has slope $-\\frac{2}{3}$ and $y$-intercept $-4$, different from $-1$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n-4x-6y=24\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27e157f0-32f6-59a2-9fc5-3469efa4bd8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x-3y=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718375} {:answer/id #uuid "355224e7-3568-50d8-8848-8e72ec543aab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+3y=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718376} {:answer/id #uuid "621155f3-3742-5a20-b5c1-fe4a0b182d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+9y=-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718377} {:answer/id #uuid "8a895ff6-8d8b-5e6e-b820-21f4e271fa03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x+3y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718378} {:answer/id #uuid "ac12a5f4-d42c-5517-be8f-c05822bad496" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+9y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "355224e7-3568-50d8-8848-8e72ec543aab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+3y=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718376} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a78029-15d0-5f15-a3eb-22a91a779e47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718374}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ead608ac-9e12-551f-80c4-842255e1e1f1" :question/problem "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $-2x-2y=6$?" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $-2x-2y=6$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x-2y &= 6 \\\\\n-2y &= 2x+6 \\\\\ny &= -x-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-1$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9x+3y=3 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-3x+1 \\\\\n3x+3y=15 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-x+5 \\\\\n-3x-3y=9 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-x-3 \\\\\n6x+9y=-36 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-4 \\\\\n6x+9y=0 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{2}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $-3x-3y=9$ has both the same slope $-1$ and the same $y$-intercept $-3$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $3x+3y=15$ has slope $-1$ and $y$-intercept $5$, different from $-3$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n3x+3y=15\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel Lines Given in Standard Form"}]}
